column14:
@umer_61161
There are many valuable experiences, I get from this voyage, like how to work like a team member, my communication skills, and English speaking is improved, and the best thing is collaborating people around the world of same field.

@florinrosoga
The collaboration and synergy among team members were the highlights of our experience. Sharing diverse ideas enhanced our project & fostered a learning environment. 

@florensi
Team support and assistance at every stage of project development. Sharing ideas. Communication and interaction in general. 

@sharafcs50
Communication between the team which helped to integrate different parts of code to come up with a working product

@soos3882
Being able to create solutions and ideas for the team and achieve project requirements.

column15:
@umer_61161
I think most of the things, seem easy to me. But the thing like communicating to the team member in English is the hardest part for me.

@florinrosoga
Balancing the demands of the project with my job responsibilities and personal life was the most challenging aspect for me. Managing time effectively to contribute to the project, while also fulfilling my professional and personal obligations, required significant effort and adaptability. 

@florensi
Uneven distribution of load within the project, which is associated with a minimal share of the time of individual participants. Reluctance to improve something, having enough time left, although a lot can be improved. 

@sharafcs50
Integrating different languages - python libraries and code inside Javascript 

@soos3882
Not being more open and friendly about sharing ideas related to the project.

column16:
Hello Chingu Team, this is Voyage 48, Tier 1, Team 2 here and we would love to express our gratitude, respect, and appreciation for giving us this amazing journey and opportunity to meet with a diverse nationality of professionals working towards achieving a common goal and exchanging skills, collaborating to solve complex issues, and learning more about one another to grow and gain experience for our future roles. Thank you once again.

And additionally we have collected comments of all of us that we would love to share:
@umer_61161
I am very happy that, we are going to complete this voyage successfully, feel great and blessed to work with the great minded people @ksenia @Florin @SOOS @ShaRaF and @Nadiia .

@florinrosoga
I'm grateful for the opportunity to work on this project and appreciate the support and resources provided. This experience has not only sharpened my technical skills and, especially, my ability to work as a cohesive team in a virtual setting.

@florensi
The main thing in the project is communication and the opportunity to share problems together to find solutions, which helps to grow and develop as a developer. When tasks are distributed within a team, it helps to complete the project on time. And also the presence of design greatly facilitates the further development of the application.

@sharafcs50
Overall a good experience, learnt how to collaborate on github with a team.

@soos3882
Overall, I enjoyed being in a team where there is constant communication and responsiveness to the project goal and objectives. Everyone was doing their tasks assigned to them and was able to share their experiences with their task and what was going well/not going well and how the issues were being solved during the sprint meetings.

